{"code":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify","tips":[{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74060","section":"Flat white bollard","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=GjXzV5Mt3vTxWvZcIAQMjQ&viewpoint=-32.7396843%2C150.9357675&heading=217.67&pitch=-5.3799999999999955","text":"White plastic bollard with red reflector near the top on front side, white/grey on the back Bollard itself is a slip rectangle with slightly rounded edges","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74060","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-b2b12c42a90630552411.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74039","section":"Bollard with red strip","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=XQPHsh5CnValoPEbD1M1jQ&viewpoint=-39.56790744061227%2C176.76394562502242&heading=339.7157905568649&pitch=-10.909543177380016","text":"Red strip around the bollard near the top with a small hole in it on the front side Sometimes with yellow or white reflectors","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74039","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-775dcacf414749aee3bf.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74045","section":"New Zealand Chevron Sign Border","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=mqvBgtcCVSunQZH4AN-7gA&viewpoint=-40.32326914109924%2C175.74704399159805&heading=238.77672038017673&pitch=-6.911481785264883","text":"A black and yellow chevron sign. - Key Detail: This New Zealand sign has a thin black border. - Distinction: Similar signs in Australia do not have this thin black border.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74045","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-bf01d6678b1f13504845.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74037","section":"Australian Black and Yellow Chevron","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=iiKWHs4gULvadLi3tfR1wQ&viewpoint=-17.475812917026012%2C145.4809057672853&heading=305.564329750255&pitch=-0.053272527918053925","text":"Australian roads use black-and-yellow chevrons They guide drivers around obstacles or sharp turns","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74037","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-bef56d8fefbf8b804601.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74040","section":"Australian Road Lines","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=gI2-zuderYYcFEVryn6vyQ&viewpoint=-31.2347906%2C136.376644&heading=272.03&pitch=6.099999999999994","text":"Australian roads use almost exclusively white road lines. Contrast: Other countries like New Zealand or South Africa use yellow lines. Note: New Zealand can also have all white lines.","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74040","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-b020234970ac7e505f9f.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74043","section":"New Zealand Road Lines","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=55lmiCbnUYLN51BiVm6rKg&viewpoint=-39.76772857783817%2C174.6546997279353&heading=276.1852958546821&pitch=-12.182570500712387","text":"Line Colors: New Zealand roads can feature both white and yellow lines, or a combination of both. Contrast: This differs from Australia, where roads use only white lines.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74043","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-6fbf70db0bd76a29a645.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74046","section":"White Triangle Road Marking","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=Q7_f6zx55_HRY2dmR0-GOQ&viewpoint=-37.66034824360537%2C175.52107126339783&heading=42.56840910390281&pitch=-32.62843204053663","text":"A white triangle is painted on the road surface. This marking tells drivers to give way to other traffic. Location: These New Zealand road markings are not found in Australia.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74046","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-d1d26633f282f693748d.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74044","section":"New Zealand Give Way Sign","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=mD0khjv9yiLelTJHL9iyiQ&viewpoint=-44.00232543260612%2C171.5700044248573&heading=343.8835030189649&pitch=0.11841727445522565","text":"Sign Type: New Zealand give way signs are a red triangle. Lettering: The letters are red. This is different from Australian give way signs, which have black letters.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74044","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-342ed364477c656fc6ec.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74059","section":"Australian Give Way Signs","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=4yelFYng3SR1fCWVdVwOLw&viewpoint=-32.9242629%2C151.7416332&heading=59.95969653570776&pitch=-0.3656300421797738","text":"Australian give way signs have a white border and black text. Contrast: New Zealand signs use red text. Similar: South African signs look the same, but you will rarely see them.","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74059","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-5ea929c94f5f1f394b1b.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74051","section":"New Zealand Highway Shields","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=aKylonTVJYvftBMMzt8Q5A&viewpoint=-37.684207251944734%2C175.21754468116973&heading=334.32309863103524&pitch=-0.8007449696214621","text":"New Zealand highway shields have a Background: red. They display Digits: white numbers. This helps distinguish them from Australian highway shields. Australian signs use letters, yellow text, and no red background.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74051","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-4da4ac29b80445ae3b1b.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74058","section":"Green Intersection Signs","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=9LiNHQjdLtPKRZegUWLPZQ&viewpoint=-32.66937255238675%2C151.83408557994144&heading=215.42154600842983&pitch=-0.20053058103746935","text":"Green signs with white arrows appear at intersections to indicate nearby towns or cities. They sometimes include the distance to the destination in kilometres.","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74058","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-00d40cadb83876bf9c64.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74057","section":"Australian Speed Limit Signs","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=6_QUIQXQRZ8iNoLA-eNOLw&viewpoint=-32.9411242%2C151.7062396&heading=214.11&pitch=0.6800000000000068","text":"Design: Australian speed limit signs have black numbers within a red circle. This circle is placed on a large white rectangular background. Contrast: New Zealand speed limit signs usually do not have this white rectangular background.","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74057","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-aafc4adeac692cbb86b6.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74042","section":"White Painted Signposts","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=TZxW_APLqCiQXph8zoTDdw&viewpoint=-37.8810861044018%2C175.9146150979522&heading=38.29348841996511&pitch=-4.0289821788675795","text":"White painted signposts are very common in New Zealand. Appearance: They can be of any shape or material. Contrast: You will not find these white signposts in Australia.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74042","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-348073f5e1a8541fe0cf.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74056","section":"Green Poles","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=B4VS1VfE9mbZqnG5zeoQVQ&viewpoint=-33.7133225%2C150.9649031&heading=172.10515129160999&pitch=5.2955616037087765","text":"Appearance: These green wooden poles are cylindrical. They are common in Australia. Similar: New Zealand uses similar poles, but South Africa does not.","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74056","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-ff27b48feac4729ff332.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74049","section":"New Zealand Concrete Poles","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=xqny4PCacCMHPcAVQTwE5w&viewpoint=-39.1909673518254%2C174.62474262068812&heading=190.7749763391727&pitch=20.0013772502989","text":"New Zealand utility poles are often made of concrete. Shape: They are typically squarish with a long indent along one side. Guard: A distinctive silver opossum guard is often visible near the top.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74049","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-dcc7602b21e2a812ec7d.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74052","section":"New Zealand Blue Street Signs","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=mRl9YL8eEZTC1Vw2blCORQ&viewpoint=-36.912510992072306%2C174.8983013546271&heading=215.86698577803338&pitch=1.7084653276521635","text":"New Zealand street signs have a blue background and white letters. This color combination is a common feature across the country. Contrast: This specific color combination is not found on street signs in Australia.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74052","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-e3e1d605caa27b032ace.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74038","section":"Australian Mailboxes","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=-g1YDiPsHCysF_1jKs4k-g&viewpoint=-32.8891611%2C151.2588991&heading=172.32871595978355&pitch=-7.97940966064165","text":"Australian mailboxes are typically red and feature a rounded top. They often display white text and a white logo. This distinct combination helps identify them in the country.","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74038","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-677073ec9baf42ad3159.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74048","section":"New Zealand Snow-Capped Mountains","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=265wjGDQjg8cfpe96LIwhg&viewpoint=-44.17993918076459%2C170.19580713696746&heading=352.59726570491756&pitch=2.5751677005175395","text":"Observe snow-capped mountains in the landscape. Comparison: New Zealand's mountains are typically taller and more rugged than those found in Australia or South Africa, serving as a distinct geographical clue.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74048","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-ce8660bcb3970b73e90c.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74053","section":"Australia-only brands","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=GQHGEMr5atj8_GiW9Aj2MA&viewpoint=-33.8511851%2C150.8987266&heading=334.15&pitch=-0.519999999999996","text":"Some brands like Hungry Jack's are present only in Australia That it is literally Burger King in Australia, so if you see Burger King, it cannot be Australia","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74053","image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-f843970c98b97b682065.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74041","section":"New Zealand Gen 3 Short Antenna","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=fntYieBrUQ5dOWAP1-5VJg&viewpoint=-40.407112%2C175.605891&heading=169.428762858251&pitch=-32.62557288258049","text":"New Zealand Google cars from Generation 3 have a short antenna at the rear. Contrast: Australian Generation 3 cars have a long antenna.","countryCodes":["NZ"],"sourceTagId":"74041","temporallySensitive":true,"image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-c768817daaac6210ec4f.avif"},{"id":"geocoach-new-zealand-vs-australia-how-to-identify-74055","section":"Australian Gen 3 Long Antenna","mapUrl":"https://www.google.com/maps/@?map_action=pano&pano=bH6AnNHnSWP4DzHOGaip8A&viewpoint=-12.470187855540509%2C130.97696548561723&heading=322.6942481346484&pitch=-34.87727695811255","text":"Long antenna on the back of the car in Generation 3 imagery Contrast: New Zealand's Generation 3 cars have a short antenna.","countryCodes":["AU"],"sourceTagId":"74055","temporallySensitive":true,"image":"meta-courses/images/geocoach-c21d77e0fb58e00f5807.avif"}]}